     {q:"What is true about the corresponding sides of similar triangles?", options:["They must be different shapes","They have no relationship","They are proportional to each other","They are always exactly equal"], answer:2},
     {q:"If one triangle has sides twice as long as a similar triangle, the scale factor is ___.", options:["2","4","0.5","1"], answer:0},
     {q:"What is true about the corresponding angles of similar triangles?", options:["They are always different","They are equal","They cannot be measured","They must add up to 90 degrees"], answer:1},
     {q:"Why are similar triangles useful in real life?", options:["They cannot be used for measurement","They only apply to art","They help with tasks like measuring height using shadows","They have no real-world use"], answer:2}
